# dumps
# Measured reflection data recovered from a real session. reflection/, catalog/ and cxx/ are
# the evidence plan/TODO.md cites — they are the difference between "we measured this" and
# "someone has to boot the game and measure it again", so they ship. The rest is scratch.
#
# cxx/ is DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED. It is UE4SS's own CXXHeaderDump of the installed binary —
# 1579 headers carrying every UFunction's real signature, and the single most useful artifact
# in this project's history: give, take, spawning, DataTable reads, status effects and skill
# lists were all diagnosed from it. But it is reverse-engineered class declarations from a
# commercial game's shipping executable, which is a different thing from the row data in
# catalog/ and the name lists in reflection/, and it does not belong in a public repository.
#
# Regenerate it locally in one action — UE4SS GUI console, "Dump CXX Headers" — and it lands in
# Pal/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/CXXHeaderDump/. dumps/cxx/README.md (also untracked) explains how to
# read it. Every fact this tree took FROM it is quoted inline at the call site with a file:line
# citation, so no finding depends on having the dump to hand.
dumps/*
!dumps/reflection/
!dumps/catalog/
# Written into the DEPLOYED copy by tools/deploy.sh so a stale in-game run is visible in
# the log. Never part of the source tree.
Scripts/palforge/build.lua
